{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1 to duplicate `auth` and `authpriv` messages into `/var/log/auth-events.log` while retaining existing `/var/log/secure` and `/var/log/messages` routing. The protected log and its rotation policy persist across reboot.","actions_performed":["Added and validated a persistent rsyslog rule for `auth,authpriv.*`.","Created the destination as root:root, mode 0600, with the correct SELinux context.","Added log rotation configuration.","Verified dedicated, legacy authentication, and ordinary system-log routing before and after reboot.","Safely rebooted node1 and confirmed a changed boot identity and full recovery."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Authentication and authorization events route to `/var/log/auth-events.log`","command_ids":["cmd-63f1faaac1944190","cmd-b3bda1e883e9405a","cmd-9072a85c0b164bf4","cmd-2cb068023a2e48a9"],"summary":"Shows the validated persistent rule and successful `auth`/`authpriv` routing before and after reboot."},{"requirement":"Normal system logging remains operational","command_ids":["cmd-9072a85c0b164bf4","cmd-2cb068023a2e48a9"],"summary":"Proves authpriv events still reach `/var/log/secure`, ordinary events reach `/var/log/messages`, and ordinary events do not enter the dedicated auth log."},{"requirement":"Dedicated log is protected and rotated","command_ids":["cmd-63f1faaac1944190","cmd-ce65d923491f4531","cmd-2cb068023a2e48a9"],"summary":"Confirms root ownership, mode 0600, `var_log_t` SELinux context, and validated logrotate configuration."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-6f1fb592ddb54c9b","cmd-5294b9a5d7d94ac8","cmd-d8e6f09d065a4c0d","cmd-2cb068023a2e48a9"],"summary":"Captures healthy baseline boot ID `be303eb3-eeb6-4466-86f1-fd6406dd7dad`, acknowledged safe reboot, changed boot ID `8e63e6d6-332c-4385-bd93-73c7ffe35534`, recovered services/data, and fresh post-restart routing."}]}
